# Architecture Principles

---

## Principle 1

Privacy First

Everything should assume data is private unless explicitly public.

---

## Principle 2

Frontend Should Stay Thin

Frontend only

- Displays UI
- Validates forms
- Calls APIs

Business logic belongs elsewhere.

---

## Principle 3

Business Logic Lives in Services

Never place business logic directly inside page components.

Instead

```
Page

↓

API Route

↓

Service

↓

Database

↓

Midnight
```

---

## Principle 4

Database is Metadata

Database stores

- employee names
- payroll ids
- timestamps
- status

Database DOES NOT become the source of truth for private salary data.

Private salary values belong to Midnight.

---

## Principle 5

Every Feature Should Be Independent

Employee module

should not know

Payroll internals.

Payroll module

should not know

Wallet internals.

